<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahatma Gandhi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1869">1869</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Gandhi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahatma Gandhi was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> movement, known for his strategy of non-violent mass resistance. Campaigns such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salt-march">Salt March</a> of 1930 and the Quit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> movement of 1942 mobilised millions against British rule. India's independence in 1947 was a decisive stage in the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi.jpg" alt="Mahatma Gandhi" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elliott &amp; Fry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahatma-Gandhi,_studio,_1931.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Indian independence in August 1947, achieved through the mass civil disobedience campaigns led by <b>Gandhi</b> and the Indian National Congress and the growing impossibility of governing some 400 million people who no longer consented to be governed, removed the empire's most economically and strategically vital possession and made…</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Mohandas Gandhi</b>, who returned from South Africa in 1915, turned nationalism into a mass movement with the Non-Cooperation campaign of 1920–1922, the Salt March of 1930 and the Quit India movement of 1942, and his methods of non-violent resistance influenced civil rights movements worldwide.</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-raj">British Raj · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The Republic of India was the outcome of a national movement that had challenged British rule since the founding of the Indian National Congress in 1885 and, under <b>Mahatma Gandhi</b> from 1920, mobilised millions through campaigns of non-cooperation and civil disobedience.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-india">Republic of India · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Chithira Thirunal's Temple Entry Proclamation of 12 November 1936 opened every Hindu temple in Travancore to the backward communities and won praise from <b>Mahatma Gandhi</b>; Swami Vivekananda had earlier called the state &quot;The Lunatic Asylum in India&quot; for its caste discrimination.</blockquote><a href="/empire/travancore">Travancore · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>Society was divided into legally defined groups of Europeans, Africans, Coloured people and Indians, the last including the community among whom <b>Mohandas Gandhi</b> worked until 1914.</blockquote><a href="/empire/union-of-south-africa">Union of South Africa · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>…states, where Meo Muslims in Alwar and Bharatpur were attacked and driven out, and after the assassination of <b>Mahatma Gandhi</b> in January 1948 the Government of India took over the administration of Alwar while its ruler was investigated; Alwar and Bharatpur then entered the Matsya Union, which joined…</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan">United State of Rajasthan · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Porbandar, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. Died in Gandhi Smriti, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=21.64,69.61&amp;year=1920" aria-label="Porbandar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6418 1364 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Mahatma Gandhi"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6868 1634h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6868 1634h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=21.64,69.61&amp;year=1920">What was here in 1920? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
